{"duration_api_ms":3696,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ee196c68-45e0-47bd-b98c-8309ab4839f9","total_cost_usd":0.0008277,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1621,"outputTokens":900,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1078,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0008277,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":476,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1078,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"No. Historical exchange volume reflects only secondary-market trades that have already occurred, so it can understate an ETF's true liquidity. Much of its tradable capacity lies in the creation/redemption process. Authorized participants (APs) can create or redeem shares in large blocks, typically 25,000 to 100,000 shares, by delivering or receiving the underlying basket or cash. This arbitrage keeps prices near NAV, but only when the underlying securities are liquid enough for APs to trade efficiently.\n\nOther indicators to examine:\n\n- **Quoted and effective spreads**, and their intraday variation\n- **Displayed depth** at the NBBO and across price levels\n- **Premium or discount** to intraday indicative NAV (iNAV) and end-of-day NAV\n- **Underlying basket liquidity**: constituent spreads, volume, and depth\n- **Creation/redemption activity** and shares outstanding changes\n- **Number and quality of market makers and APs**\n- **Auction and closing volume**, often dominant for passive flows\n- **Behavior during stress periods**, such as March 2020\n\nExecution outcomes for a specific order depend on current conditions and should be assessed with pre-trade analysis.","ttft_ms":2018,"type":"result","duration_ms":3130,"uuid":"a8a94bb3-b686-4810-a611-1344b4e6ce8a","ttft_stream_ms":397,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":397,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
